# --- Trained weights ------------------------------------------------------
# 44 MB each; ~12 of them. Not in git. Ship them as a GitHub Release asset if
# they need to travel.
#
# This used to say "every one is reproducible from the training script + seed
# recorded in its *_metrics.json". That is FALSE and was measured false in
# session 7 (TRAINING_LOG step 91): the same seed reproduces a run only while
# the backbone is frozen. Once it unfreezes, two runs of identical code on
# identical data diverge by up to 0.0220 val accuracy, and dropout makes even
# the frozen phase non-reproducible. A deleted checkpoint cannot be recreated -
# only a different checkpoint of similar quality can. The *_metrics.json is the
# record of what the file scored, not a recipe for rebuilding that exact file.
*.pt
*.pth
*.joblib
*.safetensors
*.bin

# --- Kept on purpose ------------------------------------------------------
# models/*_metrics.json and models/*.log ARE tracked: they are the evidence
# behind every number in the README and in TRAINING_LOG.md.
!api/models/*_metrics.json
!api/models/*.log

# --- Third-party reference notebooks --------------------------------------
# `code benifit/` is ~38 MB of downloaded Kaggle notebooks kept locally while
# session 6 mined them for ideas. Same policy as datasets and weights: they are
# somebody else's work, re-downloadable, and carry their embedded outputs.
# TRAINING_LOG steps 64-65, 74-75 and 80 record which ones were triaged, what
# was taken from each, and what was rejected - that record is the part worth
# keeping in git, and it is already here.
code benifit/

